From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:14:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Add MPEG-4 Part 2 decoding

MPEG-4 Part 2 Simple and Advanced Simple profile and H.263 baseline on
the H616, in the MPEG engine: I, P, B and GMC S-VOPs, half and quarter
sample, both quantisation types, interlaced coding. The engine decodes
one run of macroblocks at a time and parses no packet header, so a
request is a video packet, an H.263 GOB with a header or a whole VOP.

The GMC warp is computed from the sprite trajectory in the vendor
library's form. The DivX encoder bugs that change the chroma vectors
select the engine's own chroma rounding modes.

A B-VOP reads the co-located macroblocks the last I, P or S-VOP left in
one buffer: a B-VOP whose backward reference is any other picture is
refused. So are interlaced B-VOPs, whose direct mode the engine
predicts without the field distances, static sprites, sprite
brightness change, data partitioning, reversible VLC and pictures over
4080 wide, the engine's 8-bit macroblock count, or 2304 high.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
